# Databricks
.databricks/
*.dbc
# Scratch dir for `databricks bundle generate --source-dir`. That command downloads the
# WORKSPACE copy of every notebook next to the YAML it writes, and its default source-dir is
# `src` — which would overwrite the repo with the stale content the bundle exists to remove
# (I-096). It must live inside the repo (the CLI requires a path relative to the bundle root),
# so it is ignored here and deleted after each use.
.dab-scratch/

# Secrets / credentials
*.pem
*.key
.databrickscfg

# Local scratch
/tmp/
*.tmp
.venv/
scratchpad.txt
# Frontend build outputs — regenerated by scripts/build_console.sh
app/frontend/node_modules/
app/frontend/dist/
# NOT ignored: app/backend/fleetguard_api/console/ is committed because the Databricks
# Apps runtime runs no Node — the bundle must ship, not be built on deploy

# TypeScript incremental build cache
*.tsbuildinfo
/capstone-submission-requirement.pdf

# Local-only: an external review dropped into the tree, not part of the project record.
# What survives a review is the triage — docs/ISSUES.md for the fixes, docs/STATUS.md for the
# session entry INCLUDING an enumerated list of what was declined and why. The review file
# itself is an input, not a record, and keeping it in git invites a later reader to treat an
# outside opinion as a project decision. `repo-review2.md` was committed once by mistake
# (9e8ccf9) and removed in the next commit; the glob below is so the next one cannot be.
/repo-review*.md
/indexing-review.md

# Generated console screenshots. Regenerate with scripts/capture_screenshots.py against a
# local dev server on live Lakebase — see docs/EVIDENCE.md. Kept out of git deliberately:
# they are build output, they go stale the moment the UI changes, and the submission
# artefact is a zip, so they can be generated fresh at submission time instead.
/docs/screenshots/
